 "brief_summary": "This 6 arm study will evaluate the efficacy, safety, pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of multiple doses and regimens of a GLP-1 analogue in patients with type 2 diabetes who are treated with a stable dose of metformin. Patients will be randomized to receive either subcutaneous placebo, or subcutaneous GLP-1 analogue, 5mg, 10mg or 20mg weekly, or 10mg or 20mg every 2 weeks. All patients will continue on their existing metformin treatment regimen throughout the study. The anticipated time on study treatment is \\<3 months, and the target sample size is 100-500 individuals.",
 "eligibility": {
  "criteria": "Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* adult patients, 18-75 years of age;\n* type 2 diabetes mellitus, with stable metformin treatment for \\>=3 months;\n* stable weight +/-10% for \\>=3 months before screening.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* type 1 diabetes mellitus;\n* treatment with any anti-hyperglycemic medication other than metformin monotherapy during last 3 months;\n* use of weight-lowering medications in the last 3 months;\n* uncontrolled hypertension.",
  "healthy_volunteers": false,
  "maximum_age": "75 Years",
  "minimum_age": "18 Years",
